RetroArch 1.22.2: zero every setting before its constructor fills it.

Each setting constructor in menu/menu_setting.c declares its result without an
initializer and never assigns ui_type or enum_value_idx. The action, group and
subgroup constructors also leave value.target and default_value unassigned.
Those fields then hold whatever the stack held.

A Qt 6 build with desktop_menu_enable (the default) builds the desktop menu at
every start. FormLayout::add switches on ui_type for each listed setting. For
an action setting such as rewind_settings the stack value was sometimes
ST_UI_TYPE_UINT_RADIO_BUTTONS: the frontend then made radio buttons in a loop
with step 0 and never ran a frame. Sometimes it was ST_UI_TYPE_STRING_LINE_EDIT
and the frontend read the unassigned target and crashed.

RetroArch master declares the same results as "rarch_setting_t result = {0};".
This is that change for the ten constructors of the pinned release.

